The /univ feature is logging raw PNG binary data into laravel.log (IHDR/IEND appears in logs).

Find and remove any logging of:
- image bytes
- QuickChart response bodies
- downloaded PNG contents
- temporary image file contents

Only log metadata, e.g.:

Log::info('Trend chart generated', [
    'event' => $eventCode,
    'size' => strlen($imageBytes),
]);

Never log binary data.

Also investigate why /univ fails after /trend. Ensure chart generation, temporary files, Telegram sendPhoto, and HTTP responses are properly handled and cleaned up.

After fixing, clear the log and verify:
- /trend all works
- /univ works
- laravel.log contains only readable text and no PNG binary data.